@@ -1,16 +0,0 @@
-# Error snapshot allocation ownership
-
-`git_error_save` makes an owned copy of a dynamic error and its message. If the
-message allocation fails, it must release the already allocated error object.
-Both allocation failure paths continue to return `-1` and the static OOM error.
-No-error and other static errors remain allocation-free.
-
-A caller that restores a successfully saved dynamic error recovers the original
-diagnostic after cleanup. If saving fails, the supported fallback is the static
-OOM or thread-local initialization error, not the original diagnostic.
-
-`python3 scripts/tests/test_git_error_save.py` extracts the production snapshot,
-restore, free and string-duplication functions into a small C harness. Its
-allocator and thread state are simulated; it covers both allocation failures,
-normal deep-copy and restore, static errors, no error and missing thread state.
-Set `GIT_ERROR_SAVE_ASAN=1` to compile this harness with AddressSanitizer.
diff --git a/docs/security/http-proxy-ownership-2026-11-03.md b/docs/security/http-proxy-ownership-2026-11-03.md
deleted file mode 100644
index afc27c5f2ad25300e3da2f8b8acccf609b1a98c9..0000000000000000000000000000000000000000
--- a/docs/security/http-proxy-ownership-2026-11-03.md
+++ /dev/null
@@ -1,14 +0,0 @@
-# HTTP proxy stream ownership
-
-An HTTP server TLS stream can borrow its proxy stream. On connection failure,
-the server wrapper is closed before the proxy so that its shutdown cannot use
-a freed input. A retry retains the proxy as before. Cleanup saves and restores
-the original failure diagnostic, or clears a cleanup-only diagnostic when
-there was no original. Saving a dynamic diagnostic can fail on allocation, in
-which case libgit2 supplies its allocation error instead of the original.
-
-`scripts/tests/test_http_proxy_ownership.py` extracts the actual HTTP connect
-function and runs it against controlled stream callbacks. It covers borrowed
-connections, direct connections, retry, and cleanup diagnostic preservation
-in ordinary and AddressSanitizer builds. It does not make network connections
-or exercise a TLS handshake.
